hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-11 : List (List Word)
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-11 = cons "**Identity is by declaration.** `owl:sameAs` says two identifiers denote the same individual, and OWL semantics" (cons "then makes them interchangeable everywhere. The linked-data literature has documented for over a decade that this" (cons (quoted (cons "is both too strong and too weak. Halpin and colleagues' " (cons "When owl:sameAs isn't the same" (cons " (2010) showed that most" nil)))) (cons "published sameAs links assert something weaker: similarity, the same thing in a different context, or a related" (cons "thing. Because the declaration carries no account of what is preserved, every property crosses it, including" (cons "properties that shouldn't. Ontology alignment, the industrial answer, produces correspondences with confidence" (cons "scores, and nothing says what a correspondence lets you carry from one schema to the other." (cons "" nil)))))))
